+# fm1-base-teg: the Team EG platform
+
+fm1-base with two fixes on top. CYMA-1 is built on it from v1.1.1 on. Everything in it stays MPL-2.0, like fm1-base
+and felucca-bsp.
+
+## Base
+
+| | Commit | What it is |
+|---|---|---|
+| fm1-base ([charlesvestal/fm1-base](https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-base)) | `086cd0c` | bsp -> b413cd8: memset and memcpy a word at a time (felucca-bsp#6) |
+| bsp: felucca-bsp ([hugelton/felucca-bsp](https://github.com/hugelton/felucca-bsp)) | `b413cd8` | the merge of felucca-bsp#6 |
+
+## The fork's commits (branch `teg/platform` in both repositories)
+
+| Repository | Commit | What it changes |
+|---|---|---|
+| bsp | `7f4693a` usb.c: usb_retry in two steps | With no USB host attached (on battery, or on a charger without data lines), the main loop no longer stalls once a second. A retry was a 25 ms wait and six SIE timeouts: 29–41 ms in which keys, TRS MIDI and the screen waited. It is now two steps on separate passes, timed instead of waited, and costs 0.5–1.8 ms (fm1-emu, 205 MHz) |
+| fm1-base | bsp -> `7f4693a` | the bump |
+| fm1-base | MASTER read before the audio starts | `device/main_fm1.c` reads the MASTER pot before the audio starts, so a boot sound plays at the knob's level from its first block. It used to start at half level and fall to the pot's level about 0.25 s later |
+| fm1-base | TEG_FORK.md | this file |
+
+Unchanged:
+- the boot's USB start;
+- safe mode;
+- everything while USB is up;
+- the update loader (its `ota.bin` builds byte for byte the same);
+- the host and browser builds, which compile neither change.
+
+## Where it comes from
+
+CYMA-1's repository rebuilds this tree from the two upstream commits above and its `platform/patches/` (made with
+`git format-patch`), with `tools/get_platform.sh`.
+
+- Don't pull here, and don't run `git submodule update --remote`. The bsp gitlink records the patched commit.
+- To move to a newer upstream, apply the patches to it (felucca-bsp's in `bsp/` first), redo the bump and rebuild. The
+  package's hash then changes.
+- Once upstream has both fixes, retire this fork.
